#MCOpinion |  Singapore and Malaysia are the ‘Mexico’ of the chip supply chain for China. Jensen Huang and Nvidia will fade from the headlines but China will be at it, looking for loopholes in the US technology export restrictions

@banik_nilanjan writes : 
https://t.co/h6a8tB5wmB

Honestly confused about what Nvidia’s neocloud policy looks like now. Jensen made sure GPUs, credit, and revenue-share deals went to clouds big and small to keep the ecosystem alive. Who knows what the next CEO does.
Makes E2E Networks very interesting here—its only real dependency on Nvidia is physical GPU allocation, not cash or backstops. Given India's AI push, I think most probably that allocation continues.

@e2enetworks  should diversify to @AIatAMD otherwise their survival will be on question if Nvidia starts saying we want to deal with only big boys.

